(* ========================================================================= *)
(* Tests of the compressor models of common/snappy/snappy_compress.ml by     *)
(* evaluation: each vector is "level input output" (hex, "-" for empty),    *)
(* where output is what snappy_compress_with_level of the actual            *)
(* libsnappy.so (gcc12_O2 build of snappy 1.3.1) produced. The inputs are   *)
(* short (evaluation by rewriting is slow) but reach every phase of both    *)
(* fragment compressors: the 15-byte margin, the unrolled 16 probes, skip   *)
(* acceleration, immediate repeat matches, backtracking (level 2), long    *)
(* copies split by EmitCopy, and long literals. The models were also        *)
(* compared byte for byte with the library on several thousand inputs of up *)
(* to 140000 bytes and on all of snappy's test data, by a Python transcript  *)
(* (see FINDINGS.md).                                                        *)
(* ========================================================================= *)

